WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
A grant deadline is coming up, but your team already has

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.660
a full workload.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.460
Here is how Sharke helps you check a funder before committing

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.680
that time.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.020
Let's look at Riverbend, a fictional nonprofit.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.260
It needs funding for after-school tutoring and summer reading programs.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.580
First, we work out how much those programs need and subtract

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.680
the funding already committed.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.960
We don't count pending applications as money you have.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.420
Then we build a plan to close that gap: grants worth

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.420
applying for and funders worth getting to know.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.180
That plan is your funding pipeline.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.980
We check who those funders have supported before.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.060
For example, Dollar General's published award lists include two literacy

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.680
organizations in Durham: Augustine Literacy Project Triangle and Students to

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.680
Scholars.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:52.840
That history makes its Youth Literacy Grants worth investigating for Riverbend's

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.320
next funding cycle.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.040
We still need to confirm Riverbend meets the requirements.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.820
Next, we prepare the application materials.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.700
This draft explains Riverbend's tutoring program and flags what we still

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.360
need to confirm, including student numbers and the budget.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.360
Our Grant Office prepares the full application package for your approval.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.240
We submit it where permitted.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.080
If the funder requires you to submit it yourself, we help

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.640
you complete that step.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.520
Each month, you receive a report showing the grants and funders

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:27.240
we're pursuing, upcoming deadlines, work completed, and funding still needed.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.640
I've worked as a strategy consultant for Fortune 500 and FTSE

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.020
100 companies, and as a technology executive and an investor.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.360
Across those roles, I helped businesses decide where to put their

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.880
time and money.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.920
I've also done the grant work firsthand, winning more than one

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.410
million dollars in federal funding across several awards.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:50.160
I founded Sharke to help nonprofits build a pipeline capable of

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.720
funding their mission.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.520
We work out how big that pipeline needs to be, find

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.980
the right funding opportunities, and support the work needed to pursue

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:02.020
and win them.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.980
Grant Office starts at three hundred ninety-nine dollars a month.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.240
Your price depends on how much your organization relies on grants.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.720
Plans are month to month, and you can cancel anytime.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.700
To get started, complete a ten-minute intake and share your program

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.340
and budget materials.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.320
In the first week, we identify three to five funders worth

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.420
pursuing.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.180
We explain why each fits and show you the supporting evidence.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.200
You can also have a kickoff call with us.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.260
Visit Sharke dot A I slash grant office to choose your

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:31.600
plan.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.220
Complete a short intake, and we'll help build the pipeline and

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.400
prepare the applications to fund your mission.
